  "prose": [
    {
      "title": "Initials",
      "text": "To display initials instead of the default placeholder, set `name` prop\nto the name of the person, for example, `name=\"John Doe\"`. If the name\nis set, you can use `color=\"initials\"` to generate color based on the name:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Allowed initials colors",
      "text": "By default, all colors from the default theme are allowed for initials, you can restrict them\nby providing `allowedInitialsColors` prop with an array of colors. Note that the default colors\narray does not include custom colors defined in the theme, you need to provide them manually\nif needed.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Placeholder",
      "text": "If the image cannot be loaded or not provided, `Avatar` will display a placeholder instead. By default,\nplaceholder is an icon, but it can be changed to any React node:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Avatar.Group",
      "text": "`Avatar.Group` component combines multiple avatars into a stack:\n\nNote that you must not wrap child `Avatar` components with any additional elements,\nbut you can use wrap `Avatar` with components that do not render any HTML elements\nin the current tree, for example [Tooltip](/core/tooltip).\n\nExample of usage with [Tooltip](/core/tooltip/):\n\n  defaultElement=\"div\"\n  changeToElement=\"button\"\n  component=\"Avatar\"\n  withNext\n/>\n\nYou can combine it with [Tooltip](/core/tooltip/) or [Popover](/core/popover/) to show additional information on hover",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accessibility",
      "text": "Avatar renders `<img />` HTML element. Set `alt` prop to describe image,\nit is also used as `title` attribute for avatar placeholder when the image cannot be loaded.",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
  "parts": {
    "presence": "absent-in-official",
